diff --git a/changelog/fix_style_file_null_false_positive_for_nul.md b/changelog/fix_style_file_null_false_positive_for_nul.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..ce69e88b2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelog/fix_style_file_null_false_positive_for_nul.md
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+* [#13501](https://github.com/rubocop/rubocop/issues/13501): Fix a false positive for `Style/FileNull` when a string is `'nul'` (lowercase), which is unrelated to the Windows `NUL` null device. The `NUL` device name is now matched case sensitively. ([@dvandersluis][])
diff --git a/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/cops_style.adoc b/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/cops_style.adoc
index f33620a34..bc37742c2 100644
--- a/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/cops_style.adoc
+++ b/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/cops_style.adoc
@@ -5160,6 +5160,10 @@ OSes, `NUL` or `NUL:` on Windows), so that code is platform independent.
 Only looks for full string matches, substrings within a longer string are not
 considered.
 
+The Windows device name `NUL` is matched case sensitively (only the uppercase
+`NUL` and `NUL:` are considered), so that unrelated strings such as `'nul'` are
+not flagged. The Unix path `/dev/null` is matched case insensitively.
+
 NOTE: Uses inside arrays and hashes are ignored.
 
 [#safety-stylefilenull]
diff --git a/lib/rubocop/cop/style/file_null.rb b/lib/rubocop/cop/style/file_null.rb
